        </div>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      Whatever the number is, the judiciary is a route with stacked filters: exam rounds, then a practice or training stage, then a fixed ladder with set pay bands and less room to build income outside the post. That does not make it a poor choice, and saving and investing still build wealth. It does make it Not so scalable. If you choose it, enrol early, learn in a chamber or as a law clerk, and keep one skill that can earn if an attempt fails.
    </p>
  </div>

